From 0490109d6026caae5cbc396a5702754390ddfbf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:53:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: Wireless Mode is back on the Professional page, with
 the coupling it never had

Per radio, stock's own option sets: 2.4 GHz Auto / N only / Legacy; 5 GHz Auto /
AX only / N-AC-AX mixed / Legacy; 6 GHz Auto / AX only. A stored value outside
the set is shown as itself.

Every mode except Auto, N/AC/AX mixed and AX only makes bring-up write
wlN_11ax=0 (no HE, so no EHT either), and nothing writes it back: rc/init.c
seeds 11ax only when unset and stock hides both selects on Wi-Fi 7 platforms.
Apply now writes wlN_11ax=1 whenever the mode being applied allows HE and the
stored value is not 1, so a radio once set to N only recovers.

Locks per radio from all masters: OFDMA parked unless the mode allows HE,
AMPDU RTS and RTS Threshold parked in Legacy, Disable 802.11b parked unless
Auto. Apply confirms a mode that drops HE (new RWFP_39, 25 packs) and AX only
with stock's note. nmode_x and 11ax return to the httpd snapshot list.
